From: hashtagbasit
Subject: wifi: ath12k: WCN7860 scans by firmware range, TX kept safe

The KONKR Pocket FIT Elite and AYN Odin 3 carry a WCN7860. Its firmware
can describe two PHY frequency ranges while the driver exposes one radio,
and a scan across both missed 5 GHz networks. Split such scans at the
firmware's range boundary (only on this hardware configuration), and run
the batches while associated one channel at a time with TX paused and
drained first, so a scan doesn't drop traffic.

danyi's two patches from github.com/mydanyi/armadaos-freedom (as in
kernel-baldur 1022/1023), ported to our scan timeout, which is a wiphy
delayed work here (0036): it is cancelled in the vdev clean work only once
the last batch is done, and the next batch starts with finish_queued
cleared.

diff -ru a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -1486,6 +1486,7 @@
 	struct ath12k *ar;
 	struct ath12k_hw *ah;
 	int i, j;
+	bool scan_tx_paused;
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&ab->base_lock);
 	ab->stats.fw_crash_counter++;
@@ -1502,12 +1503,25 @@
 
 		wiphy_lock(ah->hw->wiphy);
 
+		scan_tx_paused = false;
+		for (j = 0; j < ah->num_radio; j++) {
+			ar = &ah->radio[j];
+			if (ar->scan.range_tx_paused) {
+				/* Recovery now owns the TX pause; keep the
+				 * queues stopped until the normal recovery
+				 * wake.
+				 */
+				ar->scan.range_tx_paused = false;
+				scan_tx_paused = true;
+			}
+		}
+
 		/* If queue 0 is stopped, it is safe to assume that all
 		 * other queues are stopped by driver via
 		 * ieee80211_stop_queues() below. This means, there is
 		 * no need to stop it again and hence continue
 		 */
-		if (ieee80211_queue_stopped(ah->hw, 0)) {
+		if (ieee80211_queue_stopped(ah->hw, 0) && !scan_tx_paused) {
 			wiphy_unlock(ah->hw->wiphy);
 			continue;
 		}
